WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:01.650
The Green New Deal.

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.690
The Green New Deal is not the law.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:08.010
The Green New Deal hasn't been passed in the
House and Senate and signed by the president.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.719
The Green New Deal isn't policy anywhere.

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:17.460
And yet Republicans more and more are blaming
the Green New Deal for the power failure in

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.320
Texas that we saw over the last week to 10
days.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.750
How is this possible?

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:27.560
This would be like blaming Medicare for all
for a problem when Medicare for all isn't

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.699
the law in the United States.

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:30.839
Here is an example.

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:36.080
Cancun Cruz, a Republican Texas senator Ted
Cruz, who recently fled over the US Mexico

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.630
border with his family to Mexico when the
power went out at his house in Texas, only

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:45.400
to come back twenty hours later after his
escape attempt blew up in his face.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:50.300
He was on Sean Hannity's Fox News program
last night, saying that what is to blame for

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.240
the power outages in Texas is the Green New
Deal.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.240
Take a look.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.370
We just came off of a very difficult week
where the grid failed four million Texans.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:07.630
And so we need to have a serious examination
about why that was why the grid came short.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:11.630
But one of the major elements of that is actually
the policy that Schumer is pushing for the

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:15.010
whole country, which is the Green New Deal.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:20.460
You look at Texas right now, about twenty
five percent of our electricity capacity is

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.460
wind.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.970
And yet in the middle of this storm, that
capacity dropped all the way down to two percent.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.200
You want to talk about reliability?

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:35.200
The reality was in the cold, the wind turbines
froze and the power generation wasn't there.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:42.700
Ted Cruz manages to squeeze about six lies
into that short forty second segment that

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.260
I played for you.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.800
It's a great illustration of the problem we're
talking about.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:48.990
So let's talk through it.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:55.170
First of all, what Texas did over the last
10, 15 years with their power grid.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.880
It's nothing like what the Green New Deal
would do.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:05.720
Ted Cruz wants you to believe that Texas went
all in on green energy and now has power failures.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:10.239
And it's a preview of what happens to the
whole country if the whole country.

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:14.740
Goes in the direction of green energy, Texas
did something that's the opposite of the green

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:22.299
New Deal, Texas isolated their power grid
from the rest of the country to avoid so-called

00:02:22.299 --> 00:02:26.730
federal government meddling and interference
in their energy market.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.189
Former Governor Rick Perry talked about it
last week.

00:02:29.189 --> 00:02:34.270
We've heard from a number of different people
bragging about we are an independent grid.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.379
The Green New Deal doesn't call for that.

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:40.599
And so what happened was that when the grid
was stressed and we'll talk about why it was

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:45.749
stressed, they couldn't get power from anywhere
else, has nothing to do with what is in the

00:02:45.749 --> 00:02:46.749
Green New Deal.

00:02:46.749 --> 00:02:48.730
And of course, the Green New Deal hasn't passed.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:55.799
Second, Ted says wind energy is 25 percent
of power generation capacity in Texas.

00:02:55.799 --> 00:02:57.719
This is, in theory, accurate.

00:02:57.719 --> 00:03:03.389
Texas can, in theory, get up to twenty four
point eight percent of power from wind, but

00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:04.730
that's seasonal in the winter.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:06.889
It's only a fraction of that.

00:03:06.889 --> 00:03:12.569
Last week, when the power outages happened,
25 percent of actual electricity was not coming

00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:13.610
from wind power.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:20.120
But more importantly, third, when Ted says
that energy generation capacity from wind

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.519
plummeted during the storm.

00:03:22.519 --> 00:03:23.579
That's true.

00:03:23.579 --> 00:03:30.169
But it also plummeted even more for natural
gas, coal and nuclear, on which Texas is significantly

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:31.169
more reliant.

00:03:31.169 --> 00:03:35.930
And the reason is not because of wind power
versus nuclear versus coal or gas.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:40.430
It's because Texas chose not to winterize
any of their power generation.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:45.590
So they've got an isolated grid that can't
pull from any other part of the country and

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:47.389
they opt not to Winterreise.

00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:52.489
As I've said a dozen times in the last week,
back in 2011, Texas had similar outages.

00:03:52.489 --> 00:03:58.150
A report was compiled explaining how you prevent
this in the future and they just didn't do

00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:59.150
it.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.930
And yes, some wind farms froze because they
weren't winterized.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:09.129
But the bigger problem was frozen instruments
at coal, natural gas and nuclear power plants,

00:04:09.129 --> 00:04:11.340
which are not winterized.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.749
Everything Ted Cruz is saying is a lie.

00:04:13.749 --> 00:04:19.690
Now, you might see this and write it off and
say, David, how can the Green New Deal be

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.859
to blame for anything?

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.270
It hasn't been passed.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:23.770
It hasn't been made law.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.629
No one would fall for this.

00:04:25.629 --> 00:04:27.009
And yet they do.

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:31.639
Just look at Twitter, look at Reddit, look
at the debates happening on cable news right

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:32.639
now.

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:35.910
This stuff works on lots of Republicans.

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:41.900
When Obamacare was being debated, before it
passed, there were Republicans blaming Obamacare

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:43.590
for not being able to get medical procedures.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.610
Wasn't the law yet?

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:52.509
Protesters doing things last summer were being
blamed on this is Biden's America.

00:04:52.509 --> 00:04:54.280
Trump was president.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:56.000
Millions of them fell for it.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:02.820
And this is sort of part of how they blamed
Antifa for the January 6th insurrection incited

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.680
by Trump, carried out by ists.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.580
Antifa had nothing to do with it.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:13.689
So unless time travel is a factor that I somehow
don't understand and that we've not yet been

00:05:13.689 --> 00:05:17.780
able to explain, and what we're talking about
is time moves in a different way than we conceive

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:18.889
of it.

00:05:18.889 --> 00:05:23.330
There is no possible way that the Green New
Deal is responsible, but it doesn't matter

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:24.330
to them.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:29.460
They are either falling for it or knowingly
accepting something that's untrue in order

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.970
to try to point fingers elsewhere.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:40.509
It's disgusting, but it represents a barrier
in actually getting things done properly,

00:05:40.509 --> 00:05:46.310
winterizing these electrical grids and continuing
to move to green energy, which in many ways

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:52.710
is actually more robust in its ability to
resist changes in climate and weather.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:56.830
I don't know what the future is of this talking
point, but my instinct is that it's going

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.530
to be around for a while.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:03.500
And if and when Joe Biden actually gets around
to moving forward on his Green New Deal infrastructure

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:08.189
green infrastructure plan, rather, which takes
elements from the Green New Deal, I would

00:06:08.189 --> 00:06:13.159
assume that many of these Republicans are
going to fight it by saying green New Deal

00:06:13.159 --> 00:06:16.830
type stuff is responsible for what happened
in Texas in twenty, twenty one.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.969
It'll be untrue, of course, but it's clearly
a talking point.

00:06:19.969 --> 00:06:22.539
They're going to repeat and repeat and repeat.

00:06:22.539 --> 00:06:38.469
Let me know what 

00:06:38.469 --> 00:06:53.110
you think.

00:06:53.110 --> 00:07:24.490
I'm on 
Twitter 

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:39.629
at 

00:07:39.629 --> 00:07:46.689
David Pakman,

